<title>USA: Transkaryotic places 1.7mln shrs for $55mln.</title>
<headline>Transkaryotic places 1.7mln shrs for $55mln.</headline>
<text>
<p>CAMBRIDGE, Mass., July 31 (Reuter) Transkaryotic Therapies Inc said Thursday it sold 1.7 million shares of its common stock for $55.25 million to a small number of accredited institutional investors.</p>
<p>The company said it now has about 18.4 million shares outsanding, including the 1.7 million from the recent offering. Investors paid about $32.50 a share in the offering.</p>
<p>Transkaryotic added Pacific Growth Equities Inc was the offering's placement agent.</p>
<p>The company's stock hit a new 52-week high Thursday at 34-1/2, and traded at 34-1/4 around noon, up 1.</p>
</text>
